      "writtenOn": "2026-09-15T00:50:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The socket is created with SOCK_NONBLOCK, so sendto returns immediately rather than blocking the thread. There\u0027s no co_await on the send path because there\u0027s nothing to wait for — the datagram goes straight into the kernel queue; the suspend happens on the receive side at line 188, via co_await fdio.next().\n\nVerified on hardware too: with a request outstanding, a 1s heartbeat coroutine logged for ~50s without a gap, /proc/\u003cpid\u003e/wchan stayed in do_epoll_wait rather than any socket call, and busctl introspect / GetManagedObjects / the Redfish FirmwareInventory GET all returned in milliseconds throughout.",
      "parentUuid": "b9d197de_297364b4",
      "revId": "61d8f6900cff5e333d8113af7c31e89b06d48f51",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
